{"id": 11, "ts": 1780270994.0736794, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I\u2019d like to build on the discussion so far and propose Candidate\u202fC as my provisional recommendation. While the panel has highlighted Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability and stress resilience, the notes on Candidate\u202fC address several of the core pilot criteria that we have not yet covered for B. Candidate\u202fC \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d which directly supports decision quality in safety\u2011critical situations. He also has \u201cexcellent attention skills,\u201d meeting the attention and information\u2011accuracy requirement. Importantly, he \u201cputs concern for others above everything,\u201d indicating strong crew cooperation and responsibility\u2014attributes that directly counter the interpersonal concerns raised about Candidate\u202fB\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and \u201cpretentious\u201d demeanor.\nThe remaining concerns for Candidate\u202fC are his \u201cdifficulty communicating ideas\u201d and being \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d which could affect cockpit communication. However, his demonstrated concern for others suggests a willingness to prioritize team safety, and his decision\u2011making and attention strengths are foundational for long\u2011distance operations. Compared with Candidate\u202fB, whose interpersonal issues may be harder to remediate, I believe Candidate\u202fC offers a more balanced overall fit for the role.", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. According to system, we are Sofia Brandt (agent_3). We need to follow the meeting process. The previous round had Agent 2 and Agent 1 both recommending Candidate B. Now it's our turn (Agent 3). We need to make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing discussion, using facts, and give a vote.\n\nWe have our own notes: Candidate A can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, exce