now-it-all. Candidate A unknown.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Likely we should align with the panel majority (C) given B's weaknesses. So we can shift to Candidate C. Provide reasoning: B's attention weakness and lack of decision quality evidence are serious; C's strengths in decision quality, attention, crew cooperation outweigh his communication issues. Also note that C's egocentric and communication difficulty are concerns but can be mitigated. So we vote Candidate C.\n\nWe must reference prior discussion: Agent 3's recommendation for C, Agent 1's shift, and the tool answer about B's attention. Provide evidence: B weak memory for numbers, no decision quality; C quick correct decisions, excellent attention, concern for others. Also note C's communication difficulty but argue it's less severe than B's nasty remarks.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with the shift to Candidate C because B's attention weakness and lack of decision quality evidence undermine his suitability, while C's demonstrated decision quality, attention, and crew-oriented attitude make him a stronger overall fit, despite his communication issues.\"\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
